# Problem 1
```{r}
subway_df =
  read_csv("data/NYC_Transit_Subway_Entrance_And_Exit_Data.csv") |>
  clean_names() |>
  select(
    line,
    station_name,
    station_latitude,
    station_longitude,
    starts_with("route"),
    entry,
    vending,
    entrance_type,
    ada
  ) |>
  mutate(
    entry = case_match(
      entry,
      "YES" ~ TRUE,
      "NO" ~ FALSE
    )
  )
```
The cleaned subway dataset contains 1,868 observations and 19 variables. The variables include subway line and station name, station latitude and longitude, routes served, whether entry is allowed, vending availability, entrance type, and ADA compliance. I cleaned the data by standardizing variable names, selecting only the variables relevant to this analysis, and converting the `entry` variable from character values ("YES"/"NO") to a logical variable.

These data are not completely tidy because the routes served by each station are stored across multiple columns (`route1`, `route2`, etc.), rather than in separate route number and route name variables.

```{r}
distinct_stations =
  subway_df |>
  distinct(line, station_name)

nrow(distinct_stations)
```

There are 465 distinct subway stations, where stations are identified using both `line` and `station_name`.

```{r}
ada_stations =
  subway_df |>
  filter(ada == TRUE) |>
  distinct(line, station_name)

nrow(ada_stations)
```

There are 84 ADA-compliant subway stations.

```{r}
no_vending_entry_prop =
  subway_df |>
  filter(vending == "NO") |>
  summarize(
    proportion = mean(entry, na.rm = TRUE)
  )

no_vending_entry_prop
```
Among station entrances and exits without vending, approximately 37.7% allow entrance.

```{r}
subway_long =
  subway_df |>
  mutate(
    across(starts_with("route"), as.character)
  ) |>
  pivot_longer(
    cols = starts_with("route"),
    names_to = "route_number",
    names_prefix = "route",
    values_to = "route_name"
  ) |>
  filter(!is.na(route_name)) |>
  mutate(
    route_number = as.integer(route_number)
  )

subway_long
```

```{r}
a_train_stations =
  subway_long |>
  filter(route_name == "A") |>
